,"event_uuid":"ace82217-82a0-498b-8c92-3ceba6a4a3bd","position":{"commit_sha":"543f6bcf0f6a97059eafd6d8af92258239702ac7","position":"1786748729484421001-ace82217-82a0-498b-8c92-3ceba6a4a3bd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be29f8dbeed53cc58a0dfe90704f4067dbdb82dfe14021dfd97e3f14a5ca0068","event_uuid":"22b398f4-8f3a-412f-af3c-c595fc37858f","position":{"commit_sha":"7840bd9049848d88e6581aaf6dc46197e028f6f9","position":"1786748783333008001-22b398f4-8f3a-412f-af3c-c595fc37858f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Frozen test contract card:\n- authoritative_contract: `edit_workflow` documents a loopback-only real HTTP server returning `(server, host, port, token)` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:442-463`); the operator requires individual tests be negligible without reducing behavioral coverage.\n- trigger_preconditions: numeric `127.0.0.1`, ephemeral port, built editor assets, and a `socket.getfqdn` fault injected exactly at CPython HTTPServer.server_bind's irrelevant reverse-DNS seam.\n- production_path: real `editor.edit_workflow(... serve_forever=False)` -> production server class -> real TCP bind -> real handler -> urllib GET `/workflow.bpmn`; only external name resolution is faulted.\n- test_tier: in-process integration-shaped unit with a real loopback socket/thread; a lower mocked constructor test cannot prove transport behavior remains intact.\n- observable_postcondition: resolver is never called; returned host/port exactly match the bound server address; a real GET returns BPMN XML; cleanup shuts down and closes the server.\n- collateral_invariants: literal-loopback binding, ephemeral port selection, handler request serving, token/session construction, and shutdown remain unchanged.\n- negative_control: omitted as a genuine single-point bug—the contract is that this numeric-loopback server never needs reverse DNS; existing tests cover bad Host/token and normal request behavior.\n- fault_injection: monkeypatch `socket.getfqdn` itself to raise a distinctive assertion if production reaches the proven defect seam.\n- ci_gate: default pytest tier via `make test`; node must collect and execute without skip/xfail.","timestamp":1786748317654846001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED/GREEN and safety evidence before commit:\n- RED: the final held-out oracle collected as one node and failed on current main with `AssertionError: loopback editor attempted reverse DNS for 127.0.0.1`; stack crossed `edit_workflow -> ThreadingHTTPServer -> HTTPServer.server_bind -> socket.getfqdn`.\n- Held-out GREEN: the production-only fixer never saw or touched `tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py`; after its two-file implementation, the restored oracle passed in 0.99s and completed a real `/workflow.bpmn` request.\n- Mutation proof: defect-seeding `HTTPServer.server_bind` into the new subclass returned the unchanged oracle to RED at `socket.getfqdn`; restoring `TCPServer.server_bind` returned the production diff.\n- Broader editor surface: 53 passed in 11.64s across editor, validation, and prompt-authoring modules. Worktree-venv lint passed (2023 files formatted; actionlint/zizmor/complexity/DCO clean), typecheck passed across 541 source files, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Caller-dependency sweep: CLI, unit, and e2e callers all go through `edit_workflow` and consume only server handle, bound host/port, token, serving, and shutdown. `server_name` has no consumer in src/tests, so changing it from reverse-resolved text to the literal bound address is incidental.\n- Safety: restores existing loopback behavior, adds no dependency/external call, weakens no test, and adds no skip/xfail. Construct sweep found no other production `ThreadingHTTPServer`/`HTTPServer` construction requiring this fix.","timestamp":1786748729484421001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed commit fce0fe3254 to Gerrit change 1795 immediately after local verification. Change-Id Ibadb70cbd677395a0b834888045c38ffe2a97c57; commit-ticket verification resolved full id fbd2-ab6f-625b-408a. Awaiting independent LLM-Review and Verified evidence; the macOS run is also the end-to-end replication of the original 35-second setup report.","timestamp":1786748783333008001}],"created_at":1786748124897217001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9980b6ae-aac6-468b-b6e2-47cdf610bb65","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9d6b-7628-7af9-4dcd"}],"description":"## Context\nGerrit Verify run 31846417650 dynamically attributed the recurring macOS long pole: `socket.getfqdn` consumed 35.013s inside `ThreadingHTTPServer` construction for the loopback editor fixture; constructor and fixture setup were 35.014s/35.020s. TCP bind was below the 1s instrumentation threshold. The test contract needs a real loopback HTTP server but does not consume `server_name`, so reverse DNS changes no asserted behavior. This violates the operator requirement that individual tests remain negligible and that average Verify duration stay within 20–30 minutes without reducing coverage. pip explicitly bypasses the same ~30s HTTPServer reverse-DNS path; aiohttp and urllib3 likewise bind literal loopback/raw sockets.\n\n## Proven root cause\nCPython `HTTPServer.server_bind` calls `socket.getfqdn(host)` after binding. On GitHub macOS runners, reverse resolution of numeric `127.0.0.1` repeatedly waits about 35 seconds. The editor workflow constructs `ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), ...)`, so every affected test worker pays a network-environment-dependent lookup even though only loopback bind/address behavior is contractual.\n\n## Plan\n- Inventory existing editor-server tests and freeze a held-out behavioral oracle: editor workflow starts a real loopback server even when `socket.getfqdn` raises, and still publishes the literal bound address/port needed by clients.\n- Prove the oracle RED against current main for the expected reverse-DNS reason.\n- With the oracle held out from the fixer, introduce a local ThreadingHTTPServer subclass whose bind path delegates to `socketserver.TCPServer.server_bind` and derives `server_name`/`server_port` from the already-bound literal address, matching the established pip pattern without adding a dependency.\n- Restore the oracle and prove GREEN; defect-seed the original HTTPServer bind path to return it to RED, then restore the fix.\n- Run focused editor tests, lint, typecheck, and applicable workflow/action guards.\n- Land through Gerrit, then use a full macOS Verify run to confirm the 35-second span disappears while real editor behavior remains covered.\n\n## Caller safety\nExpected post-fix behavior: all editor-workflow callers receive the same localhost URL, token, request handling, and shutdown behavior; only an unused reverse-DNS-derived `server_name` value becomes the literal bound host. Before repair, sweep all `ThreadingHTTPServer` and editor workflow callers up to three levels for any dependency on reverse-resolved `server_name`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A behavioral oracle is observed RED first because current server construction invokes `socket.getfqdn`.\n- [ ] Editor workflow starts and serves over real loopback without invoking reverse DNS.\n- [ ] Bound address/ephemeral port, request handling, authentication, and shutdown coverage remain intact.\n- [ ] No new dependency, external call, skip, xfail, or weakened assertion is introduced.\n- [ ] The defect-seeded original bind path makes the held-out oracle RED again.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, and applicable CI policy gates pass.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 precede merge.\n- [ ] A post-fix macOS Verify observation records the removed span and wall-clock effect.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_server.py","reason":"Define a literal-loopback HTTP server bind path that preserves behavior without reverse DNS."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py","reason":"Construct the editor transport with the local reverse-DNS-free server class."},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_editor.py","reason":"Hold the real loopback behavioral oracle and reverse-DNS regression coverage."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"01a586ff-58e6-49fe-b164-898eaa405d5a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","macos","editor"],"ticket_id":"fbd2-ab6f-625b-408a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Avoid reverse DNS in loopback editor test server","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cd9ec353-fafe-440d-a538-5804cd0cd2be","6609ffa8-1da5-47b7-8b72-b02d32b9e026","9980b6ae-aac6-468b-b6e2-47cdf610bb65","26ab65f4-b60e-413e-a0fc-ba123cfe7100","90cc571f-afc2-4efc-8fe3-d9a7d91af8d9","01a586ff-58e6-49fe-b164-898eaa405d5a","d5c1d8e8-161b-487d-9045-566e794fd3ab","fb160a20-f40e-4a2d-a692-bece2565f212","956977cb-25c7-4197-a0d0-cda3e2a615f8","fd5e7b0a-b261-4f44-8de8-5a5f280d8c63","ace82217-82a0-498b-8c92-3ceba6a4a3bd","22b398f4-8f3a-412f-af3c-c595fc37858f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786748783333008002,"uuid":"3aa4e064-ae57-4a4c-9828-5363f878e07f"}